{"authored" [{"question" "q-16440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{5}{-2+4\\text{i}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "1042241580bfe85bcb8ead98c499ae306eab97532c1e1ca2de711f888f510d2c" "basis" 1152 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-16440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $-2+4\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2-4\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2-4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{-2+4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5}{-2+4\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2-4\\text{i}}{-2-4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{4+8\\text{i}-8\\text{i}-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{4-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{4-16(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{4+16} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{20}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{20}=-\\frac{10}{20}-\\frac{20}{20}\\text{i}=-\\frac{1}{2}-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "1042241580bfe85bcb8ead98c499ae306eab97532c1e1ca2de711f888f510d2c" "basis" 1152 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-16440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/1401127