n" "file_sha256" "1042241580bfe85bcb8ead98c499ae306eab97532c1e1ca2de711f888f510d2c" "basis" 1152 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $-2-3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2+3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2+3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{4\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2+3\\text{i}}{-2+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\text{i}+12{\\text{i}}^{2}}{(-2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\text{i}+12(-1)}{4-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-12-8\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{-12-8\\text{i}}{13}=(-\\frac{12}{13})+(-\\frac{8}{13})\\,\\text{i}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "1042241580bfe85bcb8ead98c499ae306eab97532c1e1ca2de711f888f510d2c" "basis" 1152 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ef409593a9807a67a7c665bab6dd70eacf744d33ec4cfdb2aaa25af3d1f9dc4" "basis" 1152 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "1042241580bfe85bcb8ead98c499ae306eab97532c1e1ca2de711f888f510d2c" "basis" 1152 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "1042241580bfe85bcb8ead98c499ae306eab97532c1e1ca2de711f888f510d2c" "basis" 1152 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{3}{3+2\\text{i}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $3+2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $3-2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $3-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{3+2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{3}{3+2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{3-2\\text{i}}{3-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-6\\text{i}}{9-6\\text{i}+6\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-6\\text{i}}{9-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-6\\text{i}}{9-(4)(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-6\\text{i}}{9+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-6\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9-6\\text{i}}{13}=\\frac{9}{13}-\\frac{6}{13}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e15ed205d4eb3f92a4b2a9c2a31cb9c1d9e47ce9970a444878c4b63a522e52"} {"question" "q-541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3}{13}-\\frac{2}{13}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}-\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{13}+\\frac{2}{13}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{13}-\\frac{2}{13}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{13}-\\frac{6}{13}\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{13}-\\frac{6}{13}\\text{i}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-16440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{5}{-2+4\\text{i}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-16440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $-2+4\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2-4\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2-4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{-2+4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5}{-2+4\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2-4\\text{i}}{-2-4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{4+8\\text{i}-8\\text{i}-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{4-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{4-16(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{4+16} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{20}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{20}=-\\frac{10}{20}-\\frac{20}{20}\\text{i}=-\\frac{1}{2}-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-16440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e15ed205d4eb3f92a4b2a9c2a31cb9c1d9e47ce9970a444878c4b63a522e52"} {"question" "q-16440" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-1