an write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{16-4\\text{i}}{17}=(\\frac{16}{17})+(-\\frac{4}{17})\\,\\text{i}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-316853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e15ed205d4eb3f92a4b2a9c2a31cb9c1d9e47ce9970a444878c4b63a522e52"} {"question" "q-316853" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-316853" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{16}{17}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-316853" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-316853" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{4}{17}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{4\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}=($ {{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $-2-3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2+3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2+3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{4\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2+3\\text{i}}{-2+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\text{i}+12{\\text{i}}^{2}}{(-2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\text{i}+12(-1)}{4-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-12-8\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{-12-8\\text{i}}{13}=(-\\frac{12}{13})+(-\\frac{8}{13})\\,\\text{i}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e15ed205d4eb3f92a4b2a9c2a31cb9c1d9e47ce9970a444878c4b63a522e52"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{12}{13}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{8}{13}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-316880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{3+2\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-316880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $4\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+4\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-4\\text{i},$ or simply $-4\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3+2\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{3+2\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}}\\cdot (\\frac{-4\\text{i}}{-4\\text{i}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{-12\\text{i}-8{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-12\\text{i}-8(-1)}{-16(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-12\\text{i}}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8-12\\text{i}}{16} & =\\frac{8}{16}-\\frac{12}{16}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2})+(-\\frac{3}{4})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-316880" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e15ed205d4eb3f92a4b2a9c2a31cb9c1d9e47ce9970a444878c4b63a522e52"} {"question" "q-316880" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef53b2cff123bb3b001dfc2afa6c9ddb653b3f547b5651"} {"question" "q-316880" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066861/state.json" "file_sha256" "d5e9539f89c70be54bef5